1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
“The mysterious unknown.”

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Okay, now!

14
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[Menchi] The joy of discovering
something delicious.

15
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
And now you know what it feels like.

16
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
That feeling is
what we risk our lives for.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
SHOWDOWN x ON x THE AIRSHIP

18
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[narrator]
After clearing the Exam’s Second Phase

19
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Gon and his friends
fly through the starry sky

20
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
toward the site of the Third Phase.

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[man] I will now take the opportunity

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
to introduce myself properly
to the remaining 42 applicants.

23
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
I am Netero,

24
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
the Chairman of the Selection Committee
for this year’s Hunter Exam.

25
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
It’s a pleasure to meet all of you.

26
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
And I’m his secretary, Beans.

27
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,000
[Netero] I had originally planned

28
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
to make my appearance
during the Exam’s final phase

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
but, well seeing as how I’m already here…

30
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I have to admit,

31
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,000
there’s nothing I love more
than this feeling of tension in the air.

32
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,000
So, I think I’ll stick around
for the remainder of the trip.

33
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
[laughs]

34
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
We are scheduled
to arrive at our destination

35
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
tomorrow morning
at 8:00 a.m. exactly.

36
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
You’ll find dinner waiting for you
in the dining hall.

37
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
You’re also welcome
to get some rest, of course.

38
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
You’re free to do as you please
until we contact you.

39
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
The evening is yours.

40
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Hey come on, Gon!
Let’s go and explore the airship!

41
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Yeah!

42
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
They’ve got so much energy!

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Not me, though.
All I wanna do now is crash.

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
As do I.

45
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
However, there is one thing
that still concerns me.

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
[Leorio] Oh? What’s up?

47
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
[Kurapika] How many more phases
are there in the Exam?

48
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Huh. Yeah, they haven’t said, have they?

49
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
As long as I’ve been doing this,
it’s averaged five or six.

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Which means that we’ve still got
another three or four left to go.

51
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Well, in that case we should
get some rest now, while we can.

52
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Okay but I’d be careful if I were you.

53
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Huh?

54
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
You heard the secretary, right?

55
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
He only told us when we’re arriving.

56
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
He didn’t say
that the Third Phase of the Exam

57
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
wasn’t gonna happen right here
on the airship itself.

58
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,000
And we’ll be notified, but who knows
if that’ll be at 8:00 a.m. or not?

59
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Hold on. Are you serious?

60
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
I suppose that makes sense.

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
[Tonpa] You might wake up

62
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
and find out the Exam already took place
and you slept right through it.

63
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
If you wanna get to the next phase,

64
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
then ya better not let your guard down,
even up here. Understand?

65
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
C’mon, gimme a break.

66
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Well. Thanks for the advice. See ya later.

67
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
We’ll be sure to keep it in mind.

68
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Good luck to all of us, eh?

69
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Psyched ‘em!

70
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
I bet they’re both so nervous
they won’t sleep a wink!

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
They’ll be worthless by morning.

72
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
[Kurapika] There’s no chance
the next phase

73
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
will take place on the airship.

74
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
If that were their intention,
they wouldn’t have told us

75
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
we were free to do as we pleased
and enjoy the amenities

76
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
but to stand by and wait for instructions.

77
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
[snoring]

78
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
[tapping]

79
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
[Menchi] So. How many applicants
do you think’ll make it this year?

80
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
You mean, who’ll pass the Exam?

81
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[Menchi] Yep. Looks like we’ve got
a pretty impressive group here.

82
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Though, I did try to fail them all, sure.
But still.

83
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Gee, I don’t know.

84
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
I guess it depends on
what the other phases are.

85
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
That’s a good point.
I hadn’t thought of that.

86
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
But a few of ‘em stand out,
didn’t you notice?

87
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
And one even has this whole aura thing
going on.

88
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
What do you think, Satotz?

89
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[Satotz] I’m inclined to agree.

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
I quite like the rookies this year.

91
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Yeah! Same here!

92
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
I like number 294.

93
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
I really think he’s got a good shot
at winning.

94
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
[Satotz] I’m partial to number 99, myself.

95
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
He looks like a spoiled, selfish brat
if you ask me.

96
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
What about you, Buhara?

97
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Who I think will pass?

98
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Well, he’s not a rookie
but my money’s on number 44.

99
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I’m sure you guys must’ve noticed it, too.

100
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
but when number 255 was throwing a fit,

101
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
44 was the one who looked
like he wanted to kill somebody.

102
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
He had this cold, intense bloodlust.

103
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Menchi] Of course, I noticed that.

104
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
How could I not?

105
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
It looked like
he could barely restrain himself.

106
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Hold on, didn’t you realize?

107
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
He’s been like that
ever since we showed up.

108
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
I’ve had a bad feeling about him
this whole time.

109
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Really?

110
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Yeah.

111
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
He’s the real reason
I was so edgy during the Exam.

112
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
I mean, he kept trying
to pick a fight with me.

113
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
I had a similar experience.

114
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
He should be carefully monitored.

115
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Though it pains me to admit this,

116
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
I feel we are all birds of a feather
with him.

117
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
But his affinity for darkness,

118
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
is infinitely stronger than ours.

119
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:08,000
We Hunters, as you know,
are constantly seeking out new rivals.

120
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:12,000
And the Hunter Exam
has no shortage of opponents,

121
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:16,000
each perfectly qualified
and worthy of respect.

122
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
And every now and then in our searches
we encounter someone...

123
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Someone who chooses to surge forward

124
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
when you or I would opt for the brakes.

125
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
An anomaly of sorts.

126
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[shudders]

127
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[cook] Hey! Kids!

128
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
What are you doing?
Stay out of the kitchen!

129
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Go eat in the dining hall with the others!

130
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
[Gon and Killua grunt]

131
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
[Killua] Huh?

132
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Hey! Awesome!

133
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
-Gon, Look!
-What is it?

134
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
[Gon] Whoa!

135
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
-It’s like it’s covered in jewels!
-Yeah!

136
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
[Gon] Hey... so I was wondering…

137
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
[Killua] Huh?

138
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[Gon] Your parents. Are they--

139
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I mean… where are they?

140
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Killua] Hmm... They're alive. Probably.

141
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
[Gon] What do they do?

142
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[Killua] They're assassins.

143
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
They both are?

144
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
That’s your response?

145
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
You really are a riot, aren’t ya?

146
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
You’re not the first person
I’ve told about my parents,

147
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
but you’re the first to take it seriously.

148
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
[Gon] But it’s true, isn’t it?

149
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Why d’ya think that?

150
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
It’s just a hunch.

151
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Weird.

152
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Most of the time people only like me

153
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
because they can’t tell
if I’m serious or not.

154
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[Gon] Huh?

155
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
[Killua]
I’m from a family of assassins, so yeah,

156
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
they’re all in the business of murder.

157
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
And my entire family...

158
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
they’ve got real high hopes for me.

159
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
But, y’know… I can’t stand it.

160
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Who wants their whole life
mapped out for ‘em?

161
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
When I told them
I wanted to decide my own future,

162
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
they all flipped out. It was crazy!

163
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
My mom had tears
just streaming down her face

164
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
and she kept screaming at me

165
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
how I had the potential
to be a top assassin.

166
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Horrible parents, right?
No wonder I’m rotten!

167
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Then we started fighting,

168
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
so I slashed my mom in the face,
stabbed my brother in the side,

169
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
and ran away from home.

170
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
I’m sure they’re out for blood now.

171
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
-If they all come after me, I’ll kill ‘em!
-[laughs nervously]

172
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
When I get my license,

173
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
I’ll hunt ‘em down to the last one!

174
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
I’m willing to bet they’ve got
pretty hefty bounties on their heads.

175
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Hm?

176
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Hm...

177
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[both gasp]

178
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[Netero] Something wrong?

179
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Mr. Netero…

180
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
You didn’t see anyone
coming from that side, did you?

181
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
No, I didn’t.

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
[Killua] When did he...

183
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
You’re fast. For an old timer.

184
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Oh. That trick?

185
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
I just barely moved, that’s all.

186
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
What do you want?

187
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
You don’t have anything to do
‘til the last phase, isn’t that right?

188
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Now, now, no need to be so unkind.

189
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:55,000
I just got a little bored,
so I decided to look for some company.

190
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
By the way, I’ve been meaning to ask you,

191
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
any thoughts on your first attempt
at the Hunter Exam?

192
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Yeah! It’s a lot of fun!

193
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
There haven’t been any written tests yet,

194
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
and I was kinda worried about that.

195
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
I’m disappointed, honestly.

196
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
I expected this to be
a lot more challenging.

197
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
But I assume
the next phase’ll be more interesting.

198
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Oh, well. We’ll see…

199
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Let's go, Gon.

200
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
-Wait! Just a moment.
-[Killua] Hm?

201
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Would you like
to play a little game with me?

202
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Game?

203
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
And to make it interesting,

204
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
if you two can beat me,
I’ll make you Hunters on the spot.

205
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Really?! I’ll play!

206
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
What do you say? Well?

207
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:51,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

208
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
NETERO

209
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Now, let’s go over the rules of the game.

210
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
All you have to do is simply
take this ball away from me.

211
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
If you can do that
before the airship arrives, you win.

212
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
So, let’s see…

213
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
We’re scheduled for an 8:00 a.m. arrival,
yes?

214
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Well, that’s not too bad.
You still have nine hours left.

215
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
And feel free to use any tactics you want.

216
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
I will only defend. I promise.

217
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Huh? That’s too easy!

218
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
It’s... barely even a game!

219
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Then why not give it a try
and see if you’re right?

220
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
All we have to do is take the ball?

221
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Yes.

222
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Then, I’ll give it a shot.

223
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Go right ahead.

224
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
He thinks I’m weak.

225
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Oh?

226
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
I see a bunch of Killuas!

227
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
[Netero] One of the assassination arts…

228
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
"The Rhythm Echo."

229
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:20,000
It confuses the enemy with afterimages
created by a varying cadence of steps.

230
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,000
To think he’s already
mastered the technique at his age.

231
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
What a dreadful child!

232
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Oh wow!

233
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,000
[Killua] He sure moves around a lot.
How old is this guy?

234
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Is that all? How disappointing.

235
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
[annoyed grunt] In that case,

236
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
I’ll just have to slow him down!

237
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Ow! His pivot leg!

238
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[arrogant chuckle]

239
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[groans]

240
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[screaming in pain]

241
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
[pensive grunt]

242
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
[Netero] He certainly didn’t hold back
with that kick.

243
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,000
If I were an ordinary person,
it would have shattered my leg!

244
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
[Killua] Damn!

245
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
His legs are as hard as iron!

246
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
[grunts]

247
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Killua! Tag me, tag me!

248
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
C’mon! It’s my turn!

249
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
[pensive grunt]

250
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
[Netero] This one seems
like a very honest young man.

251
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
I’m curious to see
what he has up his sleeve.

252
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Okay!

253
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
[Netero]
Ah. I see he’s got a quick first step.

254
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
But he’s charging straight at me.

255
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Very foolish indeed.

256
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
He’s still a child…

257
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Wait, from above?

258
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[Gon] Ow!

259
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[Killua] Idiot!

260
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
We already know how high you can jump,

261
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
so you don’t have to go all out! Focus!

262
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
You had a chance!
He dropped his guard for a second!

263
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
[Netero] Heh, no kidding.

264
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
[recovering breath]

265
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
He may appear simple-minded
but he’s clearly using his head.

266
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Well, that didn’t work.

267
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[Netero] They should keep me entertained
until morning.

268
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[snoring]

269
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
[chuckles]

270
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Last time I saw those two,
they were pretty shaken up.

271
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
They were both so nervous,
I bet they aren’t getting a wink of sleep!

272
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
-[snoring]
-They’re snoring?!

273
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,000
[grunting]

274
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
[panting]

275
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[Killua grunting]

276
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[groans]

277
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Ow, ow, ow!

278
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
You boys aren’t getting anywhere, huh?

279
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Why don’t both of you
try attacking me at once?

280
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
[Killua grunts angrily]

281
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Why, you--!

282
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Okay! We gotcha now!

283
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Not bad!

284
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
But still not good enough.

285
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
[laughs]

286
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,000
[Gon]
Mr. Netero hasn’t even broken a sweat!

287
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
-Ow!
-Ow!

288
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[laughs]

289
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[Gon] If we’re gonna beat him,
we’ve got to get creative.

290
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Gotta say,
your attacks don’t amount to much.

291
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[Netero groans in pain]

292
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[Netero] What? He kicked off his shoe
to increase his range?

293
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
[grunts]

294
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
[surprised Netero groans in pain]

295
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Now’s our chance!

296
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I think not.

297
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Oh! Sneaky kids!

298
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
[both] I’ve almost got it!

299
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[both groan]

300
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Well now….

301
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Excellent teamwork!
You get an "A" for effort!

302
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
[Gon] You’re amazing, Mr. Netero!

303
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Really amazing!

304
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Ah, forget it.

305
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
I quit. Ya beat me, all right?

306
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Oh… Quitting already?

307
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Don’t quit! We’ve still got lots a time.

308
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
And besides, we came so close just now.

309
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Come on. You’re really clueless,
aren’t ya?

310
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,000
It’s hopeless.

311
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Think about it. The old guy’s barely used
his right hand or left leg.

312
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
He’s way too powerful for us, Gon.

313
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
We could keep at this for an entire year

314
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
and never get that ball.

315
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Figured it out, did you?

316
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
And here I was thinking
I’d been pretty slick about it.

317
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Oh! I get it now!

318
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
[Killua laughs]

319
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
You sure know how to piss me off, old man.

320
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Let’s go, Gon!

321
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Nah, I think I’m gonna play
a little longer.

322
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[Killua] Huh?

323
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Are you deaf? Didn’t you hear
what I just said?

324
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Look! It’s pointless!
You’ll never get the ball from him!

325
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
S’okay. ‘Cause I don’t really care.

326
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
We’ve only used up half of the time limit.

327
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
I’m gonna see if I can get him
to use his right hand

328
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
before the rest of it runs out.

329
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
I see…

330
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Fine. I get it.

331
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Well, good luck.

332
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
I’m going to bed.

333
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Hey, Mr. Netero.

334
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[Netero] Hmm?

335
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Can you tell me
how Killua did that thing he did?

336
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,000
You know, when he walked slow
and then there were a bunch of him?

337
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
That was...

338
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:16,000
a technique used by those
engaged in illegal activities.

339
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
You have no need at all to learn it.

340
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
As a matter of fact,
you should never try to learn it.

341
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
But it’s pretty impressive, huh?

342
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Hmm. It requires an incredible
amount of training to master it.

343
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Oh man, Killua really is something,
isn’t he?

344
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
-Nice try.
-[Gon chuckles nervously]

345
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,000
[Killua] Dammit. Now I’m in a bad mood.

346
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Well, it is what it is.

347
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
[number 390] Hey, kid! Wait up!

348
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[number 391] Yeah, where are your manners?

349
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
-[number 390] Hey!
-[number 391] Come back here!

350
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
If I hadn’t stopped when I did,

351
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
I probably would’ve ended up killing
the old man to get the ball.

352
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[both grunt]

353
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Ah. It looks like my little playmate
is picking up the pace a bit.

354
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Now!

355
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
He’s feinting for the ball,

356
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
but he’s really going for my stomach!

357
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Huh?

358
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
That hurt!

359
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
One more!

360
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
[Netero] Oh. If he head-butts me
in my stomach like that again,

361
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
he’ll shatter his skull!

362
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
But if I relax my muscles,
he might actually lay me out.

363
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Hmm...

364
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Best to avoid that.

365
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Ah... did that kill him?

366
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[grinning]

367
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Gotcha! You just used your right hand!

368
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Huh?

369
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
I did…

370
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
I did it! Yeah!

371
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[Gon laughing]

372
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Yay!

373
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
[snoring]

374
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
[Netero] Hello, Captain?

375
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Yes, it’s me.
Is the flight going smoothly?

376
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
I really hate to ask you to do this…

377
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Could you maybe slow the ship down?
Just a little?

378
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
[narrator] Netero had proposed the game
to kill time,

379
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
but as they played,
he saw something in Gon.

380
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:53,000
The airship and all 42
of the remaining applicants on board

381
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:57,000
are approaching the site
of the Exam’s Third Phase.

382
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

383
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Gon] Next time:

384
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
“Decision x By x Majority Rule?”

385
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
-[Killua] Major, major--
-[Gon] Major trouble!

386
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[Killua] Trouble maker!
